language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Archery: choose how many arrows to shoot at each ring so that the total score is as close as possible to the target score.
given target_score : int
$ number of rings, taken from the instance (the targets list)
given targets_dim1 : int
given targets : matrix indexed by [int(1..targets_dim1)] of int
$ the arrow count on a ring never needs to exceed the target plus the sum of all ring scores, since an optimal total is at most target plus the largest ring score
find hits : matrix indexed by [int(1..targets_dim1)] of int(0..target_score + sum(targets))
$ total score of the arrows; it is at most target plus the sum of ring scores times the arrow bound
find total : int(0..target_score + sum(targets) * 100)
minimising |total - target_score|
such that
$ the total score is the sum over the rings of the ring score times the number of arrows on that ring
total = (sum i : int(1..targets_dim1) . targets[i] * hits[i])
